Stage 2 passes the contract gate: the trusted translator reproduced `solution.mpy` byte-for-byte, and the generated program matched the literal docstring on 11,679 cases. Three canonical differences were isolated—two NaN cases and incomparable sets—and all favor the submitted program’s literal `not >=` reading, so they are observations rather than defects. I’m now rebuilding LLVM and Haskell definitions from the scratch source tree and running the auxiliary and target claims independently.
